
# Race Day — REST API Endpoint Plan

## 1. Purpose

The Race Day REST API will provide endpoints for managing users, events, event categories, participant entries and race results. The API will be implemented using C# and ASP.NET Core.

Base URL during local development: `/api`

## 2. Users

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| POST | /api/users | Register a user |
| GET | /api/users/{id} | Retrieve a user |
| PUT | /api/users/{id} | Update a user |
| DELETE | /api/users/{id} | Delete a user |

## 3. Events

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| GET | /api/events | List events |
| GET | /api/events/{id} | Retrieve event details |
| POST | /api/events | Create an event |
| PUT | /api/events/{id} | Update an event |
| DELETE | /api/events/{id} | Delete an event |

## 4. Event Categories

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| GET | /api/events/{eventId}/categories | List categories for an event |
| GET | /api/categories/{id} | Retrieve a category |
| POST | /api/events/{eventId}/categories | Create a category |
| PUT | /api/categories/{id} | Update a category |
| DELETE | /api/categories/{id} | Delete a category |

## 5. Participant Entries

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| POST | /api/entries | Enter a category |
| GET | /api/entries/{id} | Retrieve an entry |
| GET | /api/participants/{participantId}/entries | List a participant's entries |
| PUT | /api/entries/{id} | Update an entry |
| DELETE | /api/entries/{id} | Cancel an entry |

## 6. Race Results

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| POST | /api/results | Record a result |
| GET | /api/results/{id} | Retrieve a result |
| GET | /api/events/{eventId}/results | List results for an event |
| GET | /api/participants/{participantId}/results | View a participant's performance history |
| PUT | /api/results/{id} | Update a result |
| DELETE | /api/results/{id} | Delete a result |

## 7. Weather and Route Information

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| GET | /api/events/{eventId}/weather | Retrieve weather information for an event |
| GET | /api/events/{eventId}/route | Retrieve event route information |

Weather information will be retrieved from an external weather service where supported. Route information will be returned for the selected event.

## 8. HTTP Status Codes

- 200 OK: Request completed successfully.
- 201 Created: A resource was created.
- 204 No Content: Request completed without a response body.
- 400 Bad Request: Request data is invalid.
- 401 Unauthorized: Authentication is required or invalid.
- 403 Forbidden: The user lacks permission.
- 404 Not Found: The requested resource does not exist.
- 409 Conflict: The request conflicts with existing data.
- 500 Internal Server Error: An unexpected server error occurred.

## 9. Validation and Business Rules

- Required fields must be supplied.
- Email addresses must be unique.
- Only authorised organisers may manage their events.
- Categories must belong to existing events.
- Duplicate participant entries in the same category must be prevented.
- Results must reference valid entries.
- Invalid identifiers must return an appropriate error response.

## 10. Security

The API should protect passwords using secure password hashing. Authentication and role-based authorisation will be implemented according to the detailed assignment requirements.

## 11. API Testing

The API will be tested for successful requests, invalid inputs, missing resources, business rule violations and database-related behaviour. Automated tests will be run through GitHub Actions.
